<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating theoretical probability using the complement rule (at least one)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A high school in Kakamega is selecting students to represent them at the National Drama Festival. The drama club has <b>{@num_actors@} actors</b> and <b>{@num_singers@} singers</b>.</p>

[[jsxgraph width="400px" height="250px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-1, 6, 11, -1],
    axis: false, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}
});

/* Draw a simple stage area */
board.create('polygon', [[0,0], [10,0], [9,5], [1,5]], {
    fillColor: '#eceff1', fillOpacity: 0.8, 
    borders: {strokeWidth: 2, strokeColor: '#b0bec5'}
});
board.create('text', [5, -0.4, 'Drama Club Pool'], {anchorX: 'middle', fontSize: 14, strokeColor: '#455a64'});

/* Dynamically scatter the actors and singers */
var act_c = {#num_actors#};
var sing_c = {#num_singers#};

for(var i=0; i<act_c; i++) {
    var rx = 1.5 + (i * 3.1) % 7;
    var ry = 0.5 + (i * 1.7) % 4;
    board.create('point', [rx, ry], {name:'', size: 6, fillColor: '#9c27b0', strokeColor: '#4a148c'});
}

for(var j=0; j<sing_c; j++) {
    var bx = 1.5 + (j * 2.9 + 2) % 7;
    var by = 0.5 + (j * 2.3 + 1.5) % 4;
    board.create('point', [bx, by], {name:'', size: 6, fillColor: '#ff9800', strokeColor: '#e65100'});
}
[[/jsxgraph]]

<p>The principal randomly selects a delegation of exactly <b>{@select_n@} students</b>.</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Calculate the total number of possible delegations that can be formed from the entire club.</p>
<p>\(n(S) =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> To find the probability of selecting <i>at least one actor</i>, it is easier to first find the complement: selecting <b>no actors at all</b>. Calculate the number of possible delegations that consist <i>only</i> of singers.</p>
<p>\(n(\text{all singers}) =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>c) </b> Using the complement rule (\( P(\text{at least one}) = 1 - P(\text{none}) \)), determine the probability that the delegation includes <b>at least one actor</b>.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fully simplified fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P(\text{at least one actor}) =\) [[input:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: The Sample Space</b><br>
The club has a total of \({@num_actors@} + {@num_singers@} = {@total_pop@}\) students. We are choosing a delegation of \({@select_n@}\) students. Using the combinations formula:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle n(S) = {}^{{@total_pop@}}C_{{@select_n@}} = \frac{{@total_pop@}!}{{@select_n@}!({@total_pop@} - {@select_n@})!} = {@ta1@} \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: The Complement Event</b><br>
The complement of "at least one actor" is "zero actors" (meaning all \({@select_n@}\) students chosen must be singers). We calculate the combinations for choosing \({@select_n@}\) students purely from the \({@num_singers@}\) available singers:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle n(\text{all singers}) = {}^{{@num_singers@}}C_{{@select_n@}} = {@ta2@} \)</p>

<p><b>Part c: The Theoretical Probability</b><br>
First, we find the probability of the complement event (selecting no actors):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{all singers}) = \frac{n(\text{all singers})}{n(S)} = \frac{{@ta2@}}{{@ta1@}} \)</p>
<p>Then, we apply the complement rule to find our target probability:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{at least one actor}) = 1 - P(\text{all singers}) = 1 - \frac{{@ta2@}}{{@ta1@}} \)</p>
<p>Simplifying this mathematically yields:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ {@ta3@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
